    <statement><p>Let <m>y = f(x)</m> be a periodic function whose values are given below.
Find the period, amplitude, and midline.</p>
<tabular bottom="medium" left="medium" right="medium" top="medium">
<row>
<cell>x</cell>
<cell>5</cell>
<cell>25</cell>
<cell>45</cell>
<cell>65</cell>
<cell>85</cell>
<cell>105</cell>
<cell>125</cell>
<cell>145</cell>
<cell>165</cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>f(x)</cell>
<cell>17</cell>
<cell>15</cell>
<cell>-3</cell>
<cell>17</cell>
<cell>15</cell>
<cell>-3</cell>
<cell>17</cell>
<cell>15</cell>
<cell>-3</cell>
</row>
</tabular>
<p>(a) The period of the graph is <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) The midline of the graph is <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(c) The amplitude of the graph is <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>60</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>10</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



(a) The graph appears to have a period of 60.  Every change in the
<m>x</m> value of 60 brings us back to the same <m>y</m> value.



(b) The midline of the graph is 7 since
<me>\mbox{midline} = \frac{ y_{max} + y_{min} }{2} =
\frac{  17  - 3 }{2} = 7.</me>



(c) The amplitude is how much the maximum or minimum <m>y</m> value differs
from the average (midline).  Since the maximum <m>y</m> value is 17 and
the midline is 7, the amplitude is <m>17 - 7 = 10</m>.



</solution>
